# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-

"""
train_maskrcnn_detfuse_airbus_intern_winter.py

Airbus Ship Detection (Kaggle) — Mask R-CNN (torchvision) + Detector fusion (joint decision)
Target env: intern-winter (paths should be flexible; default data_dir=".")
Train size: default train_n=20000

What this script DOES (your requirements):
1) Keep your two fixes intact
   - No duplicate resize: all resizing is done ONLY by model.transform (GeneralizedRCNNTransform)
   - No double sigmoid: out["masks"] range-check; apply sigmoid at most once, and never in inst extraction

2) Use detector effectively in BOTH training and inference
   - Training: "pos-rich" sampling via detector ranking (not hard gating; just sampling bias)
   - Inference: NO hard skip by detector threshold
     Instead, use joint decision: fuse(det_prob, seg_evidence) -> decide emit or empty
     (detector low does NOT force empty if segmentation evidence is strong)

3) Threshold optimization is JOINT (共同意思決定)
   - On VAL subset, tune:
       score_thr (box score filter)
       mask_thr  (mask prob threshold)
       fusion parameters (w_det, w_seg, bias, decision_tau)
     to maximize pixel-level F2 on UNION mask (same metric skeleton you already used)

Notes:
- Metric is still pixel-union F2/IoU/Prec/Rec (same as your base). Instance-level conflict constraints for Kaggle
  (no pixel assigned to two objects) are NOT solved here — that is a separate postprocess layer.
- This is designed as a robust "mother script" (train->val tune->ptest eval->kaggle test submission).
"""

